course: dictionary
lesson: 90
title: A name with a capital letter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Adam is a name. Names of people, like Adam, Eve or Leo, are called proper nouns, and they start with a capital letter even in the middle of a sentence. «God told Adam and Eve they could eat from every tree except the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.» Here Adam is a person in the story, so he is the one being spoken to.
explain: Adam is a boy's or a man's name, and in the Bible he is the first man. The words around him give the clues: he is with Eve, and he is part of a story about a garden, a serpent and a fruit.
explain: Sometimes Adam is part of a longer phrase. «Adam's apple» is not a fruit at all. It is the bump at the front of the throat, and the name is only there because of the word's history.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Adam» is a boy's or a man's name.
fact: In the Bible, Adam is the first man.
fact: «Adam's apple» is the bump at the front of the throat.
fact: Look at the words around a name to find its clues: «Adam and Eve hid from God» tells you Adam is a person who did something.
exercise: «God told Adam and Eve they could eat from every tree except the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.» Who is Adam in this sentence? | A kind of fruit | A tree in the garden | A serpent | *A person in the story
exercise: «Adam's apple» is a bump on which part of the body? | The top of the head | The knee | The elbow | *The front of the throat
exercise: In «After eating, Adam and Eve hid from God», which word is a name? | after | eating | hid | *Adam
test: «Adam» is a name, so it starts with which kind of letter? | A small letter | A question mark | A number | *A capital letter
test: «Adam blamed Eve, and Eve blamed the serpent.» Who blamed the serpent? | *Eve | Adam | God | The children
exam: «Adam and Eve hid "because I was afraid"»: why did they hide? | *They were afraid | They were asleep | They were playing a game | They were hungry for fruit
